External avatars display as `"Avatar {ID}"` because the Avatar Open packet carries only the 8-byte persona ID — name metadata must be fetched separately via `RPersona_Cache`.

## New: `PersonaInfoCache` (`src/client/PersonaInfoCache.ts`)

Inspired by RP1Demo's `PersonaInfoAggregator` pattern:

- **Batched fetches** — requests accumulate for 500 ms, then flushed as a single batch via `pLnG.GetLnG('rp1_persona_cache')` → `Model_Open('RPersona_Cache', id)`
- **Local Map cache** — resolved names are stored and returned synchronously on subsequent lookups
- Callback-based resolution; `dispose()` cancels pending timers and clears state on logout

```ts
const cache = new PersonaInfoCache(pLnG);
cache.requestName(dwRPersonaIx, (name) => {
  avatar.name = name; // e.g. "Jane Smith" instead of "Avatar 1042"
});
```

## Integration

| Site | Behavior |
|------|----------|
| `ProximityAvatarList` | `init(proximity, cache?)` — when name stays `"Unknown"` after packet parsing, requests from cache; updates avatar entry and notifies observers on resolution |
| `ProximityAvatarListener` | Creates cache internally via `audioManager.getPLnG()`; triggers lookup when Avatar Open packet carries no `Name` field |
| `AudioVisualizer` | Constructs `PersonaInfoCache` in `attachAudioSource()`, passes to `ProximityAvatarList`, disposes alongside the list |

## Supporting changes

- `ProximityAudioManager.getPLnG()` — exposes the stored `pLnG` reference so consumers can construct a cache without a separate injection path
- `src/index.ts` — exports `PersonaInfoCache` as part of the public API

> **Note:** The cache request callback is registered *after* `this.avatars.set()` to prevent a race where a synchronous cache-hit callback runs before the avatar entry exists in the map.

